{
  "kanji": "記",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 記\ntitle: record in writing\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 言\nradicalNumber: 149\nonyomi: [キ]\nkunyomi: [しる.す]\ndistractors: [起, 計, 訪]\n---\n\n# 記 — record in writing\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 言 (no. 149) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n記 is about putting something into a written account or record. [日記](../words/日記.md) にっき is a diary;\n記録 きろく can be a record or the act of recording. Think of information retained in an account,\nnot simply any act of speaking.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine 言, words, being placed beside the curled 己 shape\nas a written note. The scene is an invented aid; it does not identify the right part as a verified phonetic.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キ | on | [日記](../words/日記.md) にっき — diary; 記録 きろく — record |\n| しる.す | kun | 記す しるす — write down |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [日記](../words/日記.md) にっき — diary; journal\n- 記録 きろく — record; recording\n- 記す しるす — note down; give an account\n\n## Notes\n\n日記 has a small っ: にっき. Do not pronounce it as にちき.\n[起](起.md) also contains 己, but its other part is different.\n[計](計.md) and [訪](訪.md) share the 言 on the left; check the entire right-hand component.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\n\nVocabulary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1463930, 1223440, 1223140.\n",
